        {
          "id": "1da9bf88-4bd1-38f5-875b-fbf7f7fcbfd8",
          "content": {
            "id": "1da9bf88-4bd1-38f5-875b-fbf7f7fcbfd8",
            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "European steelmakers' shares rise on EU plan to cut steel quotas",
            "description": "<title><body><p>STORY: Shares in European steelmakers rose in early Wednesday trade.</p><p>Investors bought up after the European Commission proposed cutting tariff-free steel import quotas by almost half.</p><p>It's part of a plan to preserve viable steelmaking in the EU.</p><p>EU steel producers are operating at only 67% of their capacity due to rising imports and U.S. tariffs.</p><p>The new measures are designed to push that up towards 80%.</p><p>ArcelorMittal said on Tuesday it was \"relieved\" by the Commission's proposal.</p><p>Thyssenkrupp also said in written statements it supported the plan, while Aperam welcomed the measures Wednesday.</p><p>Thyssenkrupp said the Commission recognized the European steel industry and its associated value chains were in serious danger without effective trade protection.</p><p>Industry data shows some 5.5 million jobs in Germany are directly or indirectly tied to the steel industry.</p><p>J.P. Morgan analysts said the proposed import quota cuts could lower steel imports into the EU by 8 metric tons.</p><p>They argue this could positively affect\u00a0local steel producers' pricing power.</p><p>But European carmakers have concerns.</p><p>The European Automobile Manufacturers' Association warned about the inflationary impact tighter restrictions could have on steel imports.</p></body></title>",
            "summary": "<body><p>STORY: Shares in European steelmakers rose in early Wednesday trade.</p><p>Investors bought up after the European Commission proposed cutting tariff-free steel import quotas by almost half.</p><p>It's part of a plan to preserve viable steelmaking in the EU.</p><p>EU steel producers are operating at only 67% of their capacity due to rising imports and U.S. tariffs.</p><p>The new measures are designed to push that up towards 80%.</p><p>ArcelorMittal said on Tuesday it was \"relieved\" by the Commission's proposal.</p><p>Thyssenkrupp also said in written statements it supported the plan, while Aperam welcomed the measures Wednesday.</p><p>Thyssenkrupp said the Commission recognized the European steel industry and its associated value chains were in serious danger without effective trade protection.</p><p>Industry data shows some 5.5 million jobs in Germany are directly or indirectly tied to the steel industry.</p><p>J.P. Morgan analysts said the proposed import quota cuts could lower steel imports into the EU by 8 metric tons.</p><p>They argue this could positively affect&nbsp;local steel producers' pricing power.</p><p>But European carmakers have concerns.</p><p>The European Automobile Manufacturers' Association warned about the inflationary impact tighter restrictions could have on steel imports.</p></body>",
